<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George V</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a>–<a href="/years/1936">1936</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as George V of the United Kingdom · Of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-windsor">House of Windsor</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George V was King of the United Kingdom and emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> from 1910 to 1936. His reign saw the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, the change of the royal house's name to Windsor in 1917, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irish-war-of-independence">Irish War of Independence</a> and the creation of the Irish Free State in 1922. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/statute-of-westminster-1931">Statute of Westminster</a> in 1931 confirmed the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">Dominions</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-v.jpg" alt="George V" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bassano Ltd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_George_1923_LCCN2014715558_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-more"><h2 class="enc-more-h">Early life and background</h2><p>George was born on 3 June 1865 at Marlborough House, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, the second son of Albert Edward, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-of-wales">Prince of Wales</a>, and Alexandra, a daughter of King Christian IX of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. As a younger son he was not expected to become king. In 1877 he and his elder brother, Prince Albert Victor, joined the training ship HMS Britannia, and he served in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> until 1892. Albert Victor's death in January 1892 made George second in line to the throne, and the next year he married his brother's former fiancée, Princess Victoria Mary of Teck. After his father became Edward VII in 1901, George was created Prince of Wales.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Reign</h2><p>George became king on 6 May 1910. He insisted that his wife be called Queen Mary, and he objected to the anti-Catholic wording of the Accession Declaration, which Parliament shortened. The Parliament Act 1911 established the supremacy of the House of Commons.</p><p>He held a council on 4 August 1914 to declare war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaiser">Kaiser</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-ii">Wilhelm II</a>, was his first cousin. Because of anti-German feeling he changed the name of the royal house in 1917 from Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> to Windsor. The monarchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, Germany, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> fell to war and revolution. On 22 June 1921, at the opening of the Parliament of Northern Ireland, he appealed for conciliation, and a truce followed within weeks. He appointed the first Labour ministry in 1924.</p><h2 class="enc-more-h">Death and legacy</h2><p>George was seriously injured in a fall from his horse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in October 1915, and heavy smoking aggravated chronic bronchitis. After a serious illness in November 1928 he convalesced at Bognor, which later gained the suffix Regis. He took to his bedroom at Sandringham House on 15 January 1936 and died on 20 January; his eldest son succeeded him as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-viii">Edward VIII</a>.</p><p>He enjoyed stamp collecting and game shooting and lived a conventional life. The historian David Cannadine describes him and Queen Mary as an inseparably devoted couple who upheld character and family values. In a series of crises he acted as a force for neutrality and moderation, seeing his role as mediator rather than final decision maker.</p><p class="enc-more-src">This account follows the Wikipedia article “George V” (CC BY-SA 4.0), linked under Read further below.</p></section>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote><b>George V</b> the Brilliant reunited the western kingdom with the rest of Georgia in 1330.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-imereti">Kingdom of Imereti · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1922 the state of about 44 million people, under King <b>George V</b> and the Conservative Prime Minister Andrew Bonar Law, still ruled the largest empire in history, held mandates over Palestine, Transjordan and Iraq, possessed the world's largest navy alongside that of the United States and was…</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom">United Kingdom · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Te Rata's delegation to England in 1914 gained an audience with King <b>George V</b> but only the assurance that its claims would be referred back to the New Zealand Government.</blockquote><a href="/movement/maori-king-movement">Māori King movement · Outcomes</a></li><li><blockquote>The hymn is sung in many Christian denominations, and King <b>George V</b> and Mahatma Gandhi were said to hold it a favourite.</blockquote><a href="/songs/abide-with-me">Abide with Me</a></li><li><blockquote>King <b>George V</b> is said to have preferred it to &quot;God Save the King&quot;.</blockquote><a href="/songs/and-did-those-feet-in-ancient-time">Jerusalem (And did those feet in ancient time)</a></li><li><blockquote>An Army Order of 1933, following <b>George V</b>'s preference, set its tempo and scoring.</blockquote><a href="/songs/god-save-the-king">God Save the King</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Marlborough House, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. Died in Sandringham House, in what is now <a href="/countries/united-kingdom">the United Kingdom</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=51.51,-0.14&amp;year=1911" aria-label="Marlborough House on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4547 381 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of George V"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4997 651h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4997 651h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=51.51,-0.14&amp;year=1911">What was here in 1911? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
